{title: Come Thou Fount}
{artist: Robert Robinson}
{key: D}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
[D]Come, thou fount of [G]every [D]blessing, tune my [G]heart to [A]sing thy [D]grace;
streams of mercy, [G]never [D]ceasing, call for [G]songs of [A]loudest [D]praise.
[A]Teach me some me[D]lodious [G]sonnet, [D]sung by [G]flaming [A]tongues a[D]bove;
praise the mount — I'm [G]fixed up[D]on it — mount of [G]thy re[A]deeming [D]love.

Verse 2
[D]Sorr'wing I shall be [G]in [D]spirit, Till [G]released from [A]flesh and [D]sin,
Yet from what [G]I [D]do inherit, Here [G]Thy praises [A]I'll [D]begin;
[A]Here I raise my [D]Ebenezer; [G]Here [D]by Thy [G]great [A]help I've [D]come;
And I hope, [G]by Thy [D]good pleasure, Safely to [G]arrive [A]at [D]home.

Verse 3
[D]Jesus sought me when [G]a [D]stranger, Wand'ring [G]from the [A]fold of [D]God;
He, to rescue [G]me [D]from danger, [G]Interposed His [A]precious [D]blood;
[A]How His kindness yet [D]pursues [G]me [D]Mortal [G]tongue [A]can never [D]tell,
Clothed in flesh, till [G]death shall [D]loose me I [G]cannot proclaim [A]it [D]well.

Verse 4
[D]O to grace how [G]great [D]a debtor [G]Daily I'm [A]constrained to [D]be!
Let Thy goodness, [G]like [D]a fetter, Bind my [G]wand'ring heart [A]to [D]Thee.
[A]Prone to wander, Lord, I [D]feel [G]it, [D]Prone to [G]leave [A]the God I [D]love;
Here's my heart, O [G]take and [D]seal it, Seal it [G]for Thy [A]courts [D]above.

Verse 5
[D]O that day when [G]freed [D]from sinning, I [G]shall see [A]Thy lovely [D]face;
Clothèd then in [G]blood [D]washed linen How [G]I'll sing Thy [A]sovereign [D]grace;
[A]Come, my Lord, no [D]longer [G]tarry, [D]Take [G]my [A]ransomed soul [D]away;
Send thine angels [G]now to [D]carry Me to realms [G]of [A]endless [D]day.
